Package: ivspatial
Type: Package
Title: Nonparametric Tests of Spatial Independence
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Emad", "Ashtari Nezhad", email = "emaad7@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-6779-4742"))
Description: Rank-based tests of the hypothesis that the values of a
    variable observed at spatial units (grid cells, polygons such as
    counties, irregularly located points or the nodes of a network) are
    independent and identically distributed. The values are replaced by
    quantile classes; orthogonal features compare the class of every site
    with those of its neighbours, in pairs and in triples, on an arbitrary
    neighbourhood graph. The combined test is calibrated exactly by random
    rank arrangements, so its P-value is valid for every sample size, every
    graph and every continuous distribution. The package also gives the
    explicit weighted chi-square null limits, standardized features that show
    whether the dependence is in the level or in the scale, local feature
    contributions for maps, a data-driven choice of the resolution with exact
    post-selection calibration, several spatial lags, tests for regression
    residuals, the screening of many variables with false discovery rate
    control, and a graphical interface. The procedure is that of Ashtari
    Nezhad, A Nonparametric Test of Spatial Independence on Neighbourhood Graphs (manuscript).
